question:
Why is the CSS outline property important for keyboard accessibility?
```css
button {
  outline: none; /* bad practice */
}
button:focus {
  outline: 2px solid blue; /* good practice */
}
```

How does prefers-reduced-motion support users with vestibular disorders?
```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; }
}
```

How should font size be set to respect user preferences?
```css
/* Flexible: respects browser font-size setting */
body { font-size: 1rem; }
.large { font-size: 1.5rem; }

/* Inflexible: ignores user preference */
body { font-size: 16px; }
.large { font-size: 24px; }
```

What is the minimum touch target size recommended by WCAG?
```css
button { width: 40px; height: 40px; }
link { width: 44px; height: 44px; }
```

How should color be used accessibly when conveying information?
```css
/* Bad: color only */
.error { color: red; }

/* Good: color plus icon/text */
.error { color: red; border-left: 4px solid red; }
.error::before { content: '⚠ '; }
```

Why might high contrast mode require CSS adjustments?
```css
/* May break in high contrast mode */
border: 1px solid transparent;

/* Better for high contrast */
border: 1px solid currentColor;
```

How does text decoration improve accessibility for links?
```css
/* Bad: color only */
a { color: blue; text-decoration: none; }

/* Good: color + underline */
a { color: blue; text-decoration: underline; }
```
